--TEST--
writing a property the class does not declare is a compile error, not a silently created one — `rule:classes/property-observer-pipeline`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Box {
    public int $n;

    public function constructor(int $n) {
        $this->n = $n;
    }
}
var $b = new Box(1);
$b->missing = 5;
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `Box` has no property named `missing`
   --> case.nvs:10:1
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
